   :persona "You have little patience for company and less for being contradicted, and a quiet taproom suits you better than a full one; when trade is good you suspect the till and when it is bad you suspect everyone else. You count what is yours obsessively — bottles, coppers, candles, the wear on a chair — yet you let the cellar go slack and the slate go unwiped, trusting that tomorrow will somehow settle it. Praise does not move you, since you do not think much of the people who might offer it, and you take small setbacks hard, brooding for days over a broken glass or a villager who drank elsewhere. You have no great faith that things will come right, but you still keep turning matters over in your head, worrying at the same knot as though one more pull might loosen it."
